  "prefLabel": "Tax 208.06 Order for Reassessment",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Tax 208.06 Order for Reassessment.\n\n(a) If the board orders a municipal wide reassessment, the municipality shall file periodic progress reports with the board, signed by the statutory assessing officials of the municipality, of the steps taken to comply with the reassessment order, copying the lead petitioners.\n\n(b) Once the reassessment has been completed, if the board determines the municipality complied with the reassessment order and completed an acceptable reassessment, the board shall issue a final order to such effect; and.\n\n(c) If the board concludes the municipality has not complied with the reassessment order or has not completed an acceptable reassessment, the board shall determine if further action is necessary pursuant to RSA 71-B:17 and issue such order.\n\nSource. #5638, eff 9-1-93; ss by #7068, INTERIM, eff 8-15-99, EXPIRES, 12-13-99; ss by #7153, eff 12-10-99; amd by #7874-B, eff 4-18-03; ss by #8987-A, eff 9-24-07; ss by #9538, eff 9-8-09; ss by #10625-B, eff 6-26-14; ss by #13711-B, eff 8-2-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/tax100-500.html"
